WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.368
We're following new tension

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.370
near the Russian border tonight.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.170
Moscow now

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.239
says its fighter jets intercepted

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.241
two American military aircraft

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.509
over the Baltic Sea.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.710
The interaction comes

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.845
amid reports of yet

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.280
another attack on Russian soil

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.082
near the Ukrainian border.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.650
CNN's Nic Robertson is joining us

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.518
now from Kiev.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.419
He's got details.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.487
Nic, what is Russia

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.422
saying about this latest incident

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.790
as it also tries

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.694
to secure the border with Ukraine?

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:28.895
Russia

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.398
saying that one of its Su 27 fighter

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.599
aircraft intercepted

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.201
what it describes as two B-1B

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.836
strategic bombers

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.371
flying over the Baltic Sea.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.440
It says it engaged with them

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.876
and according

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.845
or according to international rules, that

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.148
this was an intercept that's the way

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.283
Russia is describing it.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.484
The Pentagon is saying

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.585
that there was

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.887
an interaction

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.121
of these aircraft

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.122
in that area,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.925
that they were in international airspace,

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.261
that the interaction was safe

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.430
and professional. Nothing

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.765
to indicate at all that

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.201
it was anywhere near that

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.404
that that very dangerous interception

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.906
of Russian fighter

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:16.042
aircraft over the Black Sea with U.S.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.111
aircraft about a month or so ago.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.212
So the Pentagon

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:19.879
very clear

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.548
that this is something that happens

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:22.582
occasionally.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:26.252
Why the Kremlin is making a big deal

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.288
out of it at the moment is unclear.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.522
But certainly

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.025
the Kremlin is being embarrassed,

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.826
it appears, by

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.127
what's happened on the border

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:34.794
with Ukraine,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.495
the country it's

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.029
at war

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.097
with calls it

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.299
a special military operation.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.534
Some Russian fighters

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.069
appearing to be

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.605
have some level of support

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.273
from the government in Kiev,

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.275
although keep says that they're acting

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.343
independently, crossed

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.312
into Russia yesterday,

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.347
shot up a border area.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.815
One civilian died,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.250
according to Russian authorities.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.351
Several others were injured.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.152
But the backlash

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.187
from the Russian population in that area

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.489
was to call for that

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.924
their leaders to actually tighten up

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.126
and give them security

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:06.693
So Russia's

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.460
got this

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.595
very embarrassing

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.730
security concern on its doorstep,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.432
right at its border.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.466
Doesn't appear to have

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.901
adequate protection there.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.303
And at the same time,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.571
it does appear this evening,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:18.872
at least

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.906
according to the governor

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.175
of the Belgorod region, that

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.610
a bomb was dropped,

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.645
a small bomb was dropped from

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.947
from a drone that landed on a road.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.015
There were no casualties.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.950
There was there was some damage.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:31.651
But again,

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.486
Russia seemingly embarrassed

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.255
by cross-border activities

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.523
coming out of Ukraine.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.724
So was

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.626
the information they provided

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.627
about the intercept

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.028
to draw people's attention

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:42.595
away from that.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.664
Certainly, Russia continues

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.400
to want to pose for its population

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.668
that it's the United States

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.170
that's the threat to Russia,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.871
not Russia, the threat to Ukraine

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.940
and Ukraine's civilian population Wolf.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.941
Nic, Robertson

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.142
reporting for us from Kiev.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.443
Thank you very much.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.411
Meanwhile, in Russia

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.445
right now, the detained

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.547
American journalist

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:03.583
Evan Gross Kovic will remain in prison

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.518
until at least late August

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.753
after a court granted

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.555
Russian prosecutors more time

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:10.557
to try to build their case against him.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.291
CNN's Kelli

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.992
Atwood is on the story for us.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.359
Kylie,

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.761
what more can you tell us about

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.363
today's hearing and who attended?

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.431
Yes, that's right, Wolf.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.200
The result of today's hearing

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:20.934
was that

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.569
his pretrial detention

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.637
period is going to be extended

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.872
by about three months

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.774
until at least the end of August.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:28.441
Previously,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.610
it had been till the end of May.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.378
And so this was a request

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.113
that was made by domestic

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.149
intelligence officers in Russia,

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:36.749
who are the ones

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.951
essentially building

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.952
the case against him.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.253
We know that he is facing

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.121
charges of espionage.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:42.488
Of course,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.489
those are charges

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.057
that he

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.959
The Wall Street Journal, his family

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.126
vehemently deny.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.928
But it was really interesting

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.762
today, Wolf,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.030
that journalists weren't

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.565
allowed into the courtroom.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.666
But the folks that we did

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.200
see arrive

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.035
at that courtroom with his lawyer

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.303
or his parents

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.071
and Miscovich,

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:58.538
his parents

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:01.374
fled the Soviet Union in 1979, came here

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.209
to the United States, New York, City.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.378
They raised their family in New Jersey.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.814
So the fact that they made this bold step

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.616
to travel to Moscow

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.985
to hopefully see their son in court,

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.620
though we don't definitively know

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.520
many of the details

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.755
of what happened in that courtroom

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.257
because there weren't journalists,

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.891
is really, really interesting.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.626
And here's what

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.293
the State Department

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.028
spokesperson Matt Miller said

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.464
when responding to a question over

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.031
if the U.S.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.432
was involved at all

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.101
in their travel over to Moscow.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.571
We did not help arrange their travel.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.606
I can only imagine how difficult

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.874
it must be

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.310
to see your child detained

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.177
overseas, too,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.346
especially to be detained wrongfully.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.314
And so I'm certainly not

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:42.548
going to criticize any parent

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.018
for wanting to see their child.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.019
But that being said,

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:46.753
we do have a level

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.356
four travel advisory for Russia.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.592
And we also heard from the US embassy

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.359
in Moscow

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.461
saying that they were deeply concerned

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.330
by the court's decision today

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.365
to extend that pretrial detention period.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.433
They also pointed out,

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.734
of course, that U.S.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.503
officials have not been able to visit

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.972
Gersh Gavitt in jail for recent weeks.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.107
That request has been denied

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.876
by Russian officials Wolf.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:10.143
All right.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.444
The update from Kylie Atwood,

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.578
thank you very much.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:13.546
Let's discuss

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.147
this and more

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.448
with the former CIA

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.183
director of the former Defense Secretary,

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.017
Leon Panetta.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:18.251
Mr.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.253
Secretary, thanks so much for joining us.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.788
Let me first get your reaction

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.456
to Russia extending

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.458
Evan Herskovitz, his detention

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.327
and this decision by his parents

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:28.361
to actually go there

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.430
and attend the court proceeding

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.764
earlier today.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.166
What's your reaction to that?

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:36.469
Well,

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.572
it only confirms that

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.974
that Russia simply

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.777
has no judicial system

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:47.980
that that doesn't disregard

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.017
the rights of those that they've arrested

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.487
or it has now been extended

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.689
It's a deliberate effort,

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.992
I think, by Russia to, again,

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:02.528
send another message to the United States

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:06.032
that there in control of the situation

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.633
despite the fact

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.435
that his parents were there.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.637
It only shows you how brutal regime,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.674
Putin's regime is, how complicated Mr.

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:15.875
Secretary, are U.S.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:16.943
efforts right now

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.578
to free Avengers go back

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.713
when Russia is baselessly

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.883
accusing him of spying

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.921
It's like

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:33.092
it's from Putin's playbook as a KGB agent

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:37.864
to basically use this kind of arrest

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:40.733
to try and embarrass the United States,

00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:42.668
claiming that somehow

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.503
this Wall Street

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.605
Journal reporter is a spy,

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:48.241
which we know not to be true.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:51.210
And so he's going to basically leverage

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.946
this kind of containment

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.048
by aggressive civic

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.050
in order to try to use him

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.519
as either

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.821
someone he can trade for somebody else

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:04.557
or he's going to use it as leverage

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.192
in dealing with the United States

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:07.026
on other matters.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:09.962
So it's clearly Putin's playbook

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.831
that is working right now.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:12.398
Let's turn

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:14.534
to the latest attacks inside Russia

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.202
while I have you, Mr. Secretary.

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:17.770
These were apparently carried out

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.739
by Russian citizens.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:20.540
But is Ukraine

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.608
giving tacit approval here?

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.477
And is this a concern

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:26.479
potentially for Ukraine's allies?

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:29.849
Well, look, there's

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:30.550
no question

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.685
that the tensions

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:34.487
are increasing with Russia.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.456
What they did in intercepting

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.090
those bombers

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:41.828
in the Baltic Sea is typical provocation

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:42.795
by Russia

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.031
when they're trying to send a message.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:48.267
And the fact that that there were

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:51.103
anti-Putin, Russian militias

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:52.972
who conducted an attack

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:55.541
in Russia, in western Russia,

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:58.544
I'm sure upsets the Russians as well.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.146
And they

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:01.380
they probably believe

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.782
that Kiev is behind it,

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:03.883
although Kiev has said

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:05.952
they had nothing to do with it.

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:07.253
So we're at it.

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:09.789
We're in a tense time right now.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.424
When you when you look at everything

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:11.958
that's going

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.427
on, plus the fact that Ukraine

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:15.862
is attacking

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:18.464
other targets, largest article targets

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:19.966
to try to soften up

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:22.768
the Russians for a possible offensive

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:24.737
or all of that

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:26.005
is making things

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:27.406
very tense with the Russians.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.808
At the present time.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:30.042
The former defense secretary,

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:30.676
Leon Panetta,

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.345
thank you very much for joining us.

